# Cipher gives the creature an ability (CR 702.99a); the encoded card does not stop being encoded when the creature loses that
# ability (CR 702.99c: it ends when the card leaves exile or the creature leaves the battlefield), as the ruling says. The
# Wondrous Wasp makes Bot1's Llanowar Elves lose all abilities for as long as it stays: on turn 5 the Elves connect and
# nothing triggers (`! Bot1.Accept`) while Trait Doctoring is still in exile. Once Bot2 bolts the Wasp, the Elves have the
# ability again, and on turn 7 the same card is offered to be copied: it was encoded the whole time.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Island
Trait Doctoring
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mountain
The Wondrous Wasp
Lightning Bolt
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Trait Doctoring.Cast(Forest)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Replace a color word)
Bot1.Colors(Green)
Bot1.Colors(Blue)
Bot1.Choose(Llanowar Elves)
? Exile = Trait Doctoring
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.The Wondrous Wasp.Cast
Bot2.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = false
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves)
[T5 Bot1.CombatDamage]
? Stack.Count = 0
! Bot1.Accept
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 19
? Exile = Trait Doctoring
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.The Wondrous Wasp)
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves)
[T7 Bot1.CombatDamage]
Bot1.Decline

[Expect]
Turn = 7
Bot2.Life = 18
Exile = Trait Doctoring
Bot2.Graveyard = The Wondrous Wasp; Lightning Bolt
